# Test: an OSPF interface opting into BFD while the config has no bfd block is rejected.
#
# VALIDATES: `ze config validate` refuses a config in which an OSPF interface
#            sets `bfd { enabled true }` and no top-level bfd block exists, naming
#            the interface. An interface without bfd is not named. OSPF reads the
#            bfd root (ConfigReads) and asks the bfd plugin (api.CheckOptIns).
# PREVENTS: the adjacency running on the dead interval alone behind a doctor
#           notice, the behavior before the owner decision of 2026-10-12.

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
ospf {
    router-id 10.0.0.1
    areas {
        area 0.0.0.0 {
            area-type normal
        }
    }
    interfaces {
        interface eth0 {
            area 0.0.0.0
            bfd {
                enabled true
            }
        }
        interface eth1 {
            area 0.0.0.0
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=bfd: the config has no bfd section, so no client may opt into BFD; remove the bfd opt-in of ospf interface eth0 first
reject=stdout:contains=eth1
